{% layout 'theme' area: "home", description: home.description, path: "" %}
{% assign home = objects.home %}
{% assign product = objects.product %}

<div id="header" class="w-full flex flex-col justify-center items-center gap-6 pt-44 relative">
  <h1 class="hero-message" data-tilt-hero>
    <span class="hero-line-1">websites for</span>
    <span class="hero-line-2">everyone</span>
  </h1>
</div>

{% comment %}
  Demo video. Falls back to the poster as a plain still when no video has been
  attached yet, so the slot holds its place instead of leaving a hole under the
  hero — and the layout doesn't shift when the real video lands in the same frame.
  The still deliberately carries no play affordance: a play button that does
  nothing is worse than no button. Attaching a video to home.videos (editor or
  objects/home.toml) promotes it to a real player. With neither a video nor a
  poster, the whole section is absent.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  TEMPORARY, while Jesse finishes the video: the poster placeholder stays hidden.
  Flip this to true to bring it back before the video itself is ready. Attaching a
  real video turns the section on regardless of this flag, so nothing here needs
  remembering when the video lands.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign show_poster_placeholder = false %}

{% assign demo = home.videos | first %}
{% assign demo_file = demo.video.filename %}
{% assign has_demo = false %}
{% unless demo_file == blank %}
  {% assign has_demo = true %}
{% endunless %}
{% if show_poster_placeholder %}
  {% unless demo.poster == blank %}
    {% assign has_demo = true %}
  {% endunless %}
{% endif %}

{% if has_demo %}
  <section class="demo-video">
    <div class="demo-video-frame">
      {% if demo_file == blank %}
        <img
          class="demo-video-player demo-video-still"
          src="{{ demo.poster }}"
          alt="A site built with Archival"
          decoding="async"
        >
      {% else %}
        <video
          class="demo-video-player"
          {% if demo.poster %}
            poster="{{ demo.poster }}"
          {% endif %}
          controls
          playsinline
          preload="metadata"
        >
          <source
            src="{{ demo.video.url }}"
            name="{{ demo.video.filename }}"
            type="{{ demo.video.mime }}"
          >
        </video>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% comment %}
      The caption rides with the real video only: "in less than 10 minutes"
      alongside a still that cannot play is a promise the page can't keep.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% unless demo_file == blank %}
      {% if demo.title %}
        <p class="demo-video-caption">{{ demo.title }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    {% endunless %}
  </section>
{% endif %}

{% comment %} Build Section {% endcomment %}

<div class="build-section">
  <h2 class="build-heading">Build yours right now.</h2>

  {% comment %}
    Not hidden: the mosaic reserves its height here, in the markup, so the
    link and the CTA below it are never painted in the band's place and then
    pushed down when the catalog lands. src/index.ts hides it if the catalog
    cannot be had, and the noscript rule in the layout hides it where nothing
    will ever fill it.
  {% endcomment %}
  <div id="template-mosaic" class="template-mosaic"></div>

  <a
    id="browse-templates"
    class="browse-templates"
    href="https://editor.archival.dev/new"
    data-umami-event="hero-browse-templates"
  >
    <span>Browse all templates</span>
    <span class="browse-templates-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
  </a>

  <div class="build-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  {% include "build-cta" %}
</div>

{% comment %}
  Product tour. The .product-page wrapper is load-bearing: every callout marker
  coordinate in style/product.css is a custom property scoped to it, so the whole
  stylesheet applies here unchanged. #product is the nav's anchor target.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="product-page" id="product">
  {% for section in product.sections %}
    {% assign n = forloop.index %}
    <section
      class="product-section {% cycle 'frame-right', 'frame-left' %}"
      data-product-section
      data-section="{{ n }}"
